  "description": "Find the lowest common ancestor of two nodes p and q in a binary tree. Return null if either p or q does not exist in the tree.",
  "target": "p=5, q=4",
  "pseudocode": "1. function findLCA(root, p, q):\n2.   count = 0\n3.   result = dfs(root, p, q)\n4.   return count == 2 ? result : null\n5. function dfs(node, p, q):\n6.   if !node: return null\n7.   left = dfs(node.left, p, q)\n8.   right = dfs(node.right, p, q)\n9.   curr = (node == p || node == q) ? node : null\n10.  if curr: count++\n11.  return curr ? curr : (left ? left : right)",
